meta {
  name: Create Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "app_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "app_version_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "cluster_id": "{{clusterId}}",
    "namespace": "govchat-dev",
    "values": { "replicas": 1, "image": { "tag": "v1.0.0" } },
    "secret_inputs": { "openai_api_key": "sk-replace-me" }
  }
}

docs {
  Initiates a new deployment. Returns 202 Accepted; subscribe to /events for live progress.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; Deployer role enforced.
    2. Validate JSON shape: app_id, app_version_id, cluster_id must be valid UUIDs;
       namespace must be a DNS-1123 label (1–63 chars, lowercase alnum + hyphen).
    3. Namespace is prefixed with the last 4 chars of the caller's org UUID:
       effective_namespace = "<org_suffix>-<namespace>". Total must be <= 63 chars.
    4. App + AppVersion + Cluster must exist; AppVersion must belong to App and be published.
    5. Values validated against the version's values.schema.json: secret fields must be in
       secret_inputs, not values; required non-secret fields must be in values.
    6. Cluster scope check: caller's org must match the cluster owning org, cluster must be
       public, or caller must have a ClusterAccessGrant — 403 cluster_not_visible otherwise.
    7. Cluster must not be decommissioned — 409 cluster_decommissioned.
    8. Duplicate guard: no other non-deleted deployment of the same App in (cluster, effective_namespace) — 409.
    9. Pre-mint deployment id (UUIDv7).
    10. Each entry in secret_inputs written to SecretStore at kv/data/deployments/<id>/<field>;
        field names must match ^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]{0,62}$.
    11. Persist Deployment row (state=pending).
    12. Orchestrator.Apply() creates the Argo CD Application; on success, row → applying.
        Transient failure → pending_orchestrator (reconciler retries); permanent → failed_orchestrator.

  Responses:
    202 Accepted                   — deployment row (state=applying or pending_orchestrator)
    401 unauthorized               — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden                  — Deployer role missing or cluster inaccessible
    404 *_not_found                — app, version, or cluster not found
    409 duplicate_deployment       — same app already deployed in that cluster + namespace
    409 cluster_decommissioned     — cluster is no longer accepting deployments
    422 validation_failed          — bad UUIDs, DNS label, schema violation, or invalid secret field name
    502 orchestrator_apply_failed  — Argo CD rejected the spec
    503 orchestrator_not_configured — no ORCHESTRATOR_KIND set
    503 orchestrator_transient_error — orchestrator temporarily unavailable (deployment queued for retry)
    503 secrets_not_configured     — secret store absent and secret_inputs provided
}
